{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Sets the SECURITY groups on a library, control, or command — a deliberate permission act, distinct from tags (categorization). Empty ctl targets the library's meta.json; empty cmd targets the control record plus its inline data records; else the command's meta and impl records. Writes the comma-delimited groups string AND derives the enforced readers arrays from it (split on comma, trimmed) — the enforcement check_security/check_auth actually read. Explicit replace; empty string clears groups and derives [] (= admin-only). Library-level readers take effect on restart (system.libraries snapshot). writers is never modified. JOURNALED: a control or command change appends an entry to the control's patch journal (facet \"security\", op \"groups\", cmd = the command name or empty for the control, old/new = JSON of the groups label and readers before and after, label = \"security of <target>: <before> -> <after>\"); a library change appends one JSON line {time, author, scope, lib, old, new} to the instance-local runtime/dev/security_journal.jsonl. A call that changes nothing writes no entry. An empty author defaults to the calling session's user, else anonymous. Returns changed, groups, the derived readers, and patch_id (control/command) or journal (the file path, library) when an entry was written, or journal_warning when the change landed but could not be journaled.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\n","params":[{"name":"lib","type":"String"},{"name":"ctl","type":"String"},{"name":"cmd","type":"String"},{"name":"groups","type":"String"},{"name":"author","type":"String"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"ywwgiq19fb84a4e57h3","readers":[],"time":1795103620150,"username":"system","writers":[]}